A||||7||RoMain Stewart||Intermittent warning dinging 
Z||000000||RoMain Stewart||08-15-99||09:46 PM||||At first the intermittent dinging occured only when the AC was on, but lately it is one or two dings at no regular interval whether the AC is on or not.  Fluid levels good, door closed, hand brake completely off, seat belt fastened, guages look good, yet the dinging happens when the engine is running. It's the same dinging that is heard when the hand brake is on, yet at random times and just one or two at a time.
Z||000001||DJRice||08-16-99||07:34 AM||||The contact switch that activates the "dinger" at your hand brake could be loose or broken.  I would check that out.  <p>Your other option is to remove the dinger.  It is a small blue box under the dash on the passenger side.  It is mouned with the light flasher and horn relay
Z||000002||Bruce||08-16-99||07:09 PM||||Or, you can replace the blue control module for about $5. The Fiero Store sells them.
Z||000003||RoMain Stewart||08-16-99||10:18 PM||||Thanks guys for the suggestions.  I appreciate your interest and willingness to help.<br>Interestingly, the dinging stopped when I replaced the air filter, though the filter wasn't very dirty.
